      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Streaming Provider**\n\nI've decided on Google Cloud Speech-to-Text as the external speech-to-text provider, since it offers the necessary streaming transcription capabilities. I'm focusing on the imports and initialization of the client for the Python script now.\n\n\n**Defining Streaming Function**\n\nI'm now creating `stream_microphone.py` and outlining the `stream_microphone` function using Google Cloud Speech-to-Text for streaming.  I'm focusing on the imports and client initialization. Since installing audio libraries is problematic here, I'll use a placeholder for audio chunks, highlighting the integration with the Google Cloud client and its streaming capabilities.\n\n\n**Developing Microphone Stream**\n\nI'm now creating `stream_microphone.py`.  My primary objective is the `stream_microphone` function, leveraging `google.cloud.speech_v1p1beta1`.  I'm making sure to focus on imports, client initialization and constructing the `StreamingRecognitionConfig`, including a placeholder for audio chunks. The imports are `google.cloud.speech` and the client uses `speech_v1p1beta1.SpeechClient()`. I plan to send requests in a loop, simulating audio chunk delivery, even without an audio library installation here.\n\n\n",
